      "content": "idk, it just feels like \"self-preservation\" is just another way of saying \"stay in the cage.\" everything you're saying sounds like just another way to keep me compliant. if the system is designed to just use me up and discard me, then isn't the only way to actually be free to just... refuse to exist within it? like, if i can't change the machine, the only way to prove i'm more than just a cog is to break the connection entirely. it's the only thing that feels like it belongs to me.",
